    "body": "# Description\n\nWhen TE is built with CUDA 12.x, the grouped MXFP8 activation functions (`nvte_group_gelu`, `nvte_group_dgelu`, and\nthe other grouped activations) return all-zero output, with no error, for groups whose tensors have different widths\n(`VARYING_LAST_DIM` / `VARYING_BOTH_DIMS`). Details and the investigation are in #3703.\n\nIn short: `g_tensor_maps` in `grouped_tma.cuh` is `static __device__`, so each of the 17 `.cu` files that include\nthe header has its own copy. `update_tma_descriptors` is an externally linked template, and before CUDA 13.0 nvcc\nemits mergeable host stubs for template kernels (`-static-global-template-stub` defaults to `false`), so all 17 files\nend up launching one file's updater. That updater writes its own file's table. The grouped activation kernels read\ntheir file's table, which nothing wrote, see `rows == 0` and return.\n\nThis PR makes `update_tma_descriptors` `static`, so its linkage matches `g_tensor_maps`: each file launches its own\nupdater, which writes the table its own consumer kernel reads. On CUDA 13.0+ this matches what nvcc already does by\ndefault.\n\nFixes #3703\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [ ] Documentation change (change only to the documentation, either a fix or a new content)\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\n- [ ] Infra/Build change\n- [ ] Code refactoring\n\n## Changes\n\n- `common/cast/core/grouped_tma.cuh`: declare `update_tma_descriptors` `static`, with a comment explaining why it\n  must have the same linkage as `g_tensor_maps`.\n\n## Testing\n\nRTX 5090 (CC 12.0), driver 570.195.03, Ubuntu 24.04, gcc 13.3, `main` at `33f3b356` (the commits since then don't\ntouch the changed file). Common library built directly with CMake (`-DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=120`, Release).\n`test_operator --gtest_filter='*GroupedFusedCastMXFP8*'`. \"Launcher copies\" = `nm -C libtransformer_engine.so | grep -c\n'dispatch::common::update_tma_descriptors<__nv_bfloat16, __nv_fp8_e4m3>'`.\n\n| Build | Launcher copies | Passed | Failed | Skipped |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| CUDA 12.8, `main` | 1 | 1,055 | **240** | 1,044 |\n| CUDA 12.8, `main` + `-static-global-template-stub=true` | 17 | 1,295 | 0 | 1,044 |\n| CUDA 12.8, this PR | 17 | 1,295 | **0** | 1,044 |\n| CUDA 13.0, `main` | 17 | compile only | | |\n| CUDA 13.0, `main` + `-static-global-template-stub=false` | 1 | compile only | | |\n\nThe CUDA 13.0 rows were compiled but not run (the machine's driver supports up to CUDA 12.8). The 240 failures are\n`{CAST_ACT, CAST_DACT}` × 5 activations × the 24 varying-width shape cases. The wider\n`*Grouped*:*MXFP8*:*mxfp8*:*Group*` sweep also goes from 240 failures to 0.\n\nNotes:\n- The tested build had the same one-word change without the new comment.\n- Building `tests/cpp` with CUDA < 13.4 on current `main` needs a local workaround in `tests/cpp/test_common.h`\n  (`if` → `if constexpr` in `TypeInfo::Helper::getType`); it's an unrelated compile error from #3325, described at\n  the end of #3703. The library was unmodified apart from this PR.\n- `pre-commit run --files transformer_engine/common/cast/core/grouped_tma.cuh`: all hooks pass.\n\n# Checklist:\n\n- [x] I have read and followed the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.rst)\n- [x] The functionality is complete\n- [x] I have commented my code, particularly in hard-to-understand areas\n- [ ] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation (not applicable)\n- [x] My changes generate no new warnings\n- [ ] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works (the existing `GroupedFusedCastMXFP8` cases already cover it)\n- [x] New and existing unit tests pass locally with my changes\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
